= Individual Travel Meals & Per Diems

== Daily Meal Allowance Caps

When traveling away from the primary business location on company business, actual meal expenses are reimbursed up to daily maximum thresholds.

#policy-rule("POL-MEA-001", "Daily Meal Thresholds")[
  Reimbursement is based on actual, itemized expenditures up to the following maximum caps:
  - *Breakfast*: €15.00 / \$18.00 (reimbursable only when travel starts before 07:00 or when breakfast is not included in hotel tariff)
  - *Lunch*: €25.00 / \$30.00
  - *Dinner*: €45.00 / \$55.00
  - *Maximum Total Daily Meal Cap*: €85.00 / \$100.00
  Individual meal caps cannot be rolled over between days or accumulated across multiple meals.
]

== Prohibition of Alcohol on Solo Travel

The company maintains clear guidelines regarding alcoholic beverages consumed during individual travel.

#policy-warning("POL-MEA-002", "Solo Dining Alcohol Prohibition")[
  Alcoholic beverages (beer, wine, spirits) purchased during solo dining or individual travel meals are strictly non-reimbursable under all circumstances. If a restaurant receipt contains both food and alcoholic beverages, the cost of alcohol and corresponding proportional tax must be deducted from the claim.
]

== Gratuities and Restaurant Tips

Tips must align with local customs and standards of the host country.

#policy-rule("POL-MEA-003", "Tip and Gratuity Limits")[
  In countries where tipping is customary (such as the United States), gratuities up to a maximum of twenty percent (20%) of the meal subtotal are reimbursable. In jurisdictions where service charge or VAT is legally included (such as the European Union and Japan), tips exceeding ten percent (10%) or discretionary tips exceeding €5.00 / \$5.00 will not be reimbursed.
]
